machine: kiln_agent provider, services through the root agent

Kiln OS has BusyBox init, no systemd, and Moonraker runs as klipper, so
Fluidd's service buttons and the update manager's managed_services had
nothing to restart with (provider: none). "[machine] provider: kiln_agent"
takes the provider class from Kiln's kiln_os component: it lists klipper,
moonraker, nginx, helixscreen and ad5x-camera with their state (from the
init scripts' pid files) and hands start/stop/restart to the root update
agent (S68ad5x-update-agent), which refuses while a print runs. A
Moonraker restart waits for the agent's answer, which comes before the
agent restarts Moonraker, so a refusal reaches the caller instead of being
dropped in a background task.

Upstream: not submitted (AD5X open OS)

